; K. proton-19. period 4, group 1 alkali metal. valence: 1.
; K⁺ ion: primary intracellular cation. sodium-potassium pump drives nerve impulse.
; essential for heart muscle rhythm. plant nutrition (K, N, P are the three).
; reacts vigorously with water (more so than sodium).
; radioactive isotope K-40: naturally occurring, used in potassium-argon dating.

(kosha potassium
  (sthita element domain-chemistry domain-biology)
  (swarupa proton-nineteen alkali-metal)
  (yukta valence-one water nerve-impulse heart plant)
  (janya nuclear-fusion)
  (siddha ionic-bond))
